  "notes": "Prices are CAD MSRP excluding freight/PDI (~$2,800) and taxes, sourced primarily from Canadian Audi dealer pricing pages (Quebec dealer blogs) and AutoTrader.ca; CarCostCanada blocks automated fetch. KEY 2026 NAMING/LINEUP NOTES: (1) The former gas A4 sedan/Avant is now badged A5 in Canada (one Sportback liftback body; A5/S5 Coupe and Cabriolet are gone). Audi has publicly said it will revert to the old naming around 2029. (2) A7 and S7 (gas) are DISCONTINUED for 2026; only RS 7 performance continues. (3) The gas S6 is DISCONTINUED; the A6 gains a Sport Plus package in its place. New gas A6 is V6-only. (4) A6 e-tron / S6 e-tron are Sportback-only and quattro AWD only in Canada, and SKIP the 2026 model year (sold as 2025, return as 2027) per Automotive News - therefore NOT included as active 2026 trims; the S6 e-tron likewise resumes for 2027. (5) Q6 e-tron family: Canadian dealer pages list 2026 Q6/SQ6 e-tron (SUV + Sportback) with pricing not yet officially finalized (estimated here, med/low confidence); note Automotive News reported a 2026 skip for some North American Q6 variants, so availability/timing has some uncertainty. (6) Q8 e-tron / SQ8 e-tron are DISCONTINUED (production ended Feb 2025) - included ONLY as leftover 2025 inventory, clearly flagged, low confidence. (7) RS 5 for 2026 is uncertain: the outgoing 2.9 V6 RS 5 Coupe/Sportback (444 hp) is shown as transitional/low-confidence; an all-new PHEV RS 5 (~630 hp) launches in Europe summer 2026 and is not yet confirmed as a Canadian 2026 MY car. (8) A8 L and S8 Canadian MSRP are estimated (low confidence) - reliable CAD figures were not confirmed (some search results returned implausible low values). (9) Q3 is all-new 3rd-gen; PHEV not imported to Canada. GAPS: exact Canadian MSRP for A8 L, S8, RS e-tron GT (non-performance), Q6/SQ6 e-tron, Q5/SQ5 Sportback, and Q7 Progressiv/Technik 55 trims are estimates flagged med/low; torque figures for some EVs are null where unconfirmed."
